1
00:00:00,792 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,521
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:30,822
<i>Mama! Mama!</i>

6
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:34,451
<i>Arnaldo almost killed you!</i>
<i>Emilia tried to murder you!</i>

7
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:37,537
<i>The next time something</i>
<i>like this happens, remember,</i>

8
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,914
<i>I'll be the one</i>
<i>to take the bullet for you.</i>

9
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:41,583
<i>I'm the mayor of this place!</i>

10
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:42,917
<i>Why are you keeping me in here?!</i>

11
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:46,755
[Julio] <i>I want Arnaldo out of</i>
<i>that stinking rathole</i>

12
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:48,548
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

13
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:49,883
<i>Please tell me.</i>

14
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:52,927
<i>Who was behind all that bedlam?</i>

15
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:55,472
<i>Papa, isn't it obvious?</i>
<i>It was Ivy and Diego</i>

16
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:58,183
<i>who staged everything</i>
<i>to bring Arnaldo down.</i>

17
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:00,226
<i>So, if we are to hit back at anyone,</i>

18
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,395
<i>I want to make sure</i>
<i>we hit the right target.</i>

19
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:06,191
<i>That's Arthur Vergara,</i>
<i>one of Camia Cruz's witnesses.</i>

20
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:08,359
<i>I already regret what I did to Carlotta.</i>

21
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:10,612
<i>-What more do you want?</i>
<i>-This isn't enough!</i>

22
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:14,449
<i>I want your conscience to eat at you.</i>

23
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:16,534
<i>Send my regards to Emilia.</i>

24
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:18,953
<i>Given the fact that she wanted me killed…</i>

25
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:19,913
[Emilia] <i>I wouldn't be surprised</i>

26
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:21,247
<i>if that woman slandered me to my son.</i>

27
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,583
<i>That's why Arnaldo's so mad at me.</i>

28
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:25,043
<i>And he almost killed me!</i>

29
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:26,586
<i>We should get the head of the snake.</i>

30
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:27,921
<i>We should kill her.</i>

31
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:30,423
<i>-Ivy Aguas is better off dead.</i>
<i>-Do it.</i>

32
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,717
<i>Tell me what I can do to help you.</i>

33
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:35,804
<i>Give me Ivy. I'm begging you.</i>

34
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:41,100
Please escort Ivy Aguas to hell.

35
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:43,561
And give my regards to the devil too.

36
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:45,355
Yes, ma'am.

37
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:52,654
[car engine starts]

38
00:01:56,282 --> 00:01:57,450
How exciting.

39
00:02:00,578 --> 00:02:03,456
[tense music playing]

40
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:12,924
What's going on here?

41
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,431
Congressman.

42
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:24,769
Mrs. Emilia and Col. Sanggano
ordered us to kill Ivy Aguas.

43
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,104
[chuckles]

44
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:29,482
Sorry to disappoint you, children,

45
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:31,526
but there won't be any bloodshed today.

46
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:35,864
I need Ms. Aguas, and I need her alive.

47
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:37,699
Understood, Congressman.

48
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:48,710
Yes, ma'am.

49
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:50,461
Make sure these papers are all--

50
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:54,382
Ms. Ivy, you have to see this.
The Ardientes' men are here.

51
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:01,264
[tense music playing]

52
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:21,534
What are you doing here, Congressman?

53
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,037
We need to talk, Ms. Aguas.

54
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:27,332
[car doors open]

55
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:29,667
That's as far as you go, Congressman.

56
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:35,131
You and your army are not welcome here.

57
00:03:42,138 --> 00:03:43,681
So, what did you want to discuss?

58
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:45,558
And make it quick too.

59
00:03:46,517 --> 00:03:48,144
Okay, let's cut to the chase.

60
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,857
I'm here to make you an offer, Ivy.

61
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,235
An offer?

62
00:03:56,027 --> 00:03:58,029
A hundred million pesos.

63
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:01,866
Plus, any government position you want.

64
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:03,618
[laughing]

65
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:04,911
Seriously?

66
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:06,996
Yes.

67
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:09,624
And in exchange?

68
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:13,461
Get back together with my grandson.

69
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:17,632
Arnaldo needs you.

70
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:24,389
And if you really meant it
when you said you loved him…

71
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:28,935
And, if you really had nothing
to do with the incident…

72
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:34,857
You'll take care of him,
help him get back on his feet,

73
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:39,279
and make him feel loved
like you said you would.

74
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:40,530
There's no way I'm getting back

75
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:42,907
with the man who killed my Nanny Carlotta!

76
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:45,827
If you really love someone,

77
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:51,874
you can forgive them no matter
the mistakes they might make.

78
00:04:53,626 --> 00:04:58,214
Unless the whispers and rumors are true

79
00:04:59,632 --> 00:05:03,344
that you're betraying us
and siding with the enemy.

80
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:07,056
In that case, there's nothing
else to be discussed.

81
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,475
But then again, you know me.

82
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:11,936
You know what I'm capable of.

83
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:16,858
I can have you obliterated
from the face of this earth!

84
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:21,154
And, I'll let all your loved ones witness

85
00:05:21,237 --> 00:05:24,824
you experiencing an agonizing death.

86
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:29,078
Ivy, Ivy…

87
00:05:30,955 --> 00:05:35,126
You're courting a war
that you're not prepared for.

88
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:40,339
Or, have thought of,
even in your wildest dreams.

89
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:45,845
So please, don't push me against the wall!

90
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,473
Don't test me.

91
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,143
Do you need an answer now?

92
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:58,232
I'll think about it.

93
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:02,820
Fair enough.

94
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:06,616
But I won't wait forever.

95
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:11,245
Remember, someone in my family

96
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:13,998
desperately wants to see you dead.

97
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:18,669
And, I'm the only one
who can protect you from her.

98
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:21,130
At the end of the day,

99
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:24,759
you need me more than I need you.

100
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:31,474
And I do hope you make the right
and wise decision.

101
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:41,109
[tense music playing]

102
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,821
You're so cute, Congressman.

103
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:49,325
Very amusing.

104
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:10,888
-Well, how was your errand?
-Ma'am…

105
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:19,188
Why are you with our men, Papa?

106
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:21,065
Well, who did you expect to find anyway?

107
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:23,526
Ivy's corpse, maybe?

108
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:29,824
Ivy Aguas' funeral is postponed
until further notice.

109
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:32,201
Huh?! But why?!

110
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:35,997
My secretary will inform you
of the latest developments.

111
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:39,083
In the meantime, have a nice day.

112
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:50,094
-Auntie?
-Diego?

113
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:51,387
Anna, where's Ms. Camia?

114
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,139
Ms. Camia, Diego's here!

115
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:55,808
-Diego.
-Auntie.

116
00:07:57,059 --> 00:08:00,229
Ivy's asking me to get you.
We're going to meet her.

117
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:02,690
Really?

118
00:08:03,399 --> 00:08:06,110
-Wait, right now?
-Yes, right now.

119
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,362
Okay. I'll go get changed.

120
00:08:08,446 --> 00:08:09,906
Where does she plan to meet us?

121
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:13,284
She didn't tell me.
So get dressed, Auntie.

122
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:14,577
Okay, I'll get dressed.

123
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,204
I'm so excited to see my daughter!

124
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:17,663
Wait for me.

125
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:20,917
Diego.

126
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:23,794
Hey, what are you two waiting for?

127
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:26,422
-We're coming too?
-Of course.

128
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,549
Ivy wants to see all of us.

129
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:31,594
Hey.

130
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:48,903
-Lily!
-Mom.

131
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:52,990
[soft music playing]

132
00:08:55,743 --> 00:08:57,078
Anna.

133
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:07,171
Jepoy.

134
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:36,033
I'm happy that we're all together.

135
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,620
Now, I want to thank you all.

136
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:43,666
My plan was successful
because of all of you.

137
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:47,795
Jepoy, Diego…

138
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,506
Thank you so much.

139
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:53,968
You did everything to protect me.

140
00:09:55,761 --> 00:10:00,349
We achieved a great victory
by defeating Arnaldo,

141
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:02,435
but we aren't done yet.

142
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:05,938
That was just the beginning.

143
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:11,736
But for now, we'll celebrate.

144
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:22,997
I missed you, Lily.

145
00:10:24,498 --> 00:10:25,916
I missed you too, Mom.

146
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,796
[Emilia screaming]

147
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:37,553
[sobbing]

148
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:40,556
Emilia, what's going on?!
That's enough, already.

149
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:43,225
-Let go of me!
-What's going on?

150
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:46,187
Nothing! You don't care, right?!

151
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:48,606
Nothing's going on!

152
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:49,690
Wait…

153
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:52,401
If you're mad, don't take it out on me.

154
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:54,320
Why not? What are you
going to do about it?

155
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:56,781
I'm always the one fighting for us.

156
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:59,283
You can't even stand up
to Papa on your own!

157
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,577
That's why this is all you can do!

158
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:04,497
What are you trying to prove?
That I'm a loser?

159
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:08,417
I need a man who is my equal,
and that obviously isn't you!

160
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:10,461
Well then, let's split up already!

161
00:11:12,296 --> 00:11:13,381
You know?

162
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:17,009
I just realized, I never had
the courage to say that to you.

163
00:11:17,093 --> 00:11:20,304
Yes! I'm filing an annulment.
We're through.

164
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:24,350
Wait, Emilia. Why are you like this today?

165
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,727
Why are you acting so tough?

166
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:30,356
Do I already have a replacement?
Is it Jaguar?

167
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:35,611
Don't wait for my answer.
You might not like it.

168
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:47,706
[dramatic music playing]

169
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:08,436
[sobs]

170
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:19,196
[pensive music playing]

171
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:28,998
<i>Diego, I need to talk</i>
<i>to Arthur immediately.</i>

172
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:30,875
<i>Arthur, we need your help.</i>

173
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:33,794
<i>Ivy needs your help.</i>

174
00:12:35,671 --> 00:12:37,798
<i>Diego, I'm making changes to my plans.</i>

175
00:12:38,382 --> 00:12:42,428
<i>I'll broadcast Arnaldo's confession</i>
<i>to all of Ardiente.</i>

176
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:45,848
<i>I'll make sure your plans succeed.</i>

177
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:47,850
<i>Even if it costs me my life,</i>

178
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:50,394
<i>I won't let anything happen to you.</i>

179
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:53,230
[explosion]

180
00:12:55,691 --> 00:12:56,734
<i>Aren't you done yet?</i>

181
00:12:57,401 --> 00:13:00,029
<i>Arnaldo's reciting his vows.</i>
<i>We're running out of time!</i>

182
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:01,447
<i>Hang on, Diego.</i>

183
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:03,449
<i>I'm waiting for the right moment.</i>

184
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,160
<i>Hey! Diego!</i>

185
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,287
<i>Stop the wedding!</i>

186
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:23,135
Diego.

187
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:30,976
I'll be repeating what I said earlier,

188
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:33,437
but I want to tell you
in a more personal way…

189
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,189
Thank you.

190
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:40,319
Thank you for keeping your promise to me

191
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:44,031
that you'd help my plans succeed.

192
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:48,827
I hope you'll be with me
till the very end.

193
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:58,963
["Hindi Kita Iiwan" by Sam Milby playing]

194
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:14,061
Thank you, Diego.

195
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:19,859
Look.

196
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:46,468
Raul.

197
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:48,762
Where's your wife?

198
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:53,392
She's gone, Papa.

199
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:56,979
Emilia left me.

200
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:01,275
Are you kidding me?

201
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:05,362
No, Papa. It's true.

202
00:15:05,779 --> 00:15:06,906
Whoa.

203
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:14,955
For real? She left you?

204
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:16,999
For what reason? Why?

205
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:18,083
[chuckles]

206
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:21,795
Don't tell me it's because
you've been unfaithful again.

207
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:24,340
Because if that's the case,

208
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:27,259
she should have left you years ago.

209
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:29,136
So, that can't be the reason.

210
00:15:29,219 --> 00:15:30,804
No, I haven't cheated on her.

211
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:32,514
You didn't cheat on her?

212
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:38,479
You didn't cheat on her?

213
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:39,939
[laughs]

214
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:41,231
No…

215
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:47,446
It's the other way around?
Emilia cheated on you?

216
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:50,199
She's the cheater now?

217
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:53,619
[laughing]

218
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:54,745
Finally!

219
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:59,875
Finally, my daughter
does something good in her life!

220
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:03,003
Something that I can applaud her for!

221
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:06,256
Emilia, wherever you are, congratulations!

222
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:08,550
This is wonderful!

223
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:09,551
[laughs]

224
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:11,845
Oh wait, Raul.

225
00:16:13,138 --> 00:16:17,267
How does it feel to be given
a dose of your own medicine?

226
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:19,269
Hmm?

227
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,608
Oh, okay.

228
00:16:25,567 --> 00:16:26,819
You don't have to answer me.

229
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,031
Anyway…

230
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:36,203
Just keep it up, my son.

231
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:38,038
Who knows?

232
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:41,667
You might die ahead of me.

233
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:46,463
[grunts]

234
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:14,324
[splashes]

235
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,553
Diego, you okay there?

236
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:42,102
Is it gone?

237
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:45,022
It got away.

238
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:56,075
By the way, thank you.

239
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:59,578
For protecting and watching over Ivy.

240
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:02,289
But let me tell you this.

241
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,292
Don't get too comfy.

242
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:08,962
Because if you hurt her,

243
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:12,132
not only will you get it from me…

244
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:15,219
I'll take her from you.

245
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,054
She's in good hands with me.

246
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:18,722
Don't worry.

247
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:20,974
I hope so, bro. I hope so.

248
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:22,851
You can trust me on that.

249
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:34,321
[upbeat music playing]

250
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,157
Did you get it?

251
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:38,325
Did you?

252
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:07,020
Did you get it?

253
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:15,028
Yeah.

254
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:22,077
[upbeat music continues]

255
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:32,838
No, you didn't.

256
00:19:32,921 --> 00:19:33,922
See, bro…

257
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:38,177
Just because you have something
doesn't mean it's yours.

258
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:41,263
You need to secure it.

259
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:44,141
Get it?

260
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:54,067
-There's so much food!
-That's right! Wow!

261
00:19:58,488 --> 00:19:59,489
Oh.

262
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:02,701
Look at that, Anna!
Jepoy caught such a huge fish!

263
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,578
You're right! That is huge!

264
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:05,871
I caught everything here.

265
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:09,291
Jepoy just took it from me.

266
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:12,878
Why did you have to fight over one fish

267
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:14,963
when there are
so many fishes in the river?

268
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:17,633
Just like Lily. People fight over her.

269
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:20,302
What?

270
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:22,804
What did you say?

271
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:24,848
[chuckles] Nothing, Auntie.

272
00:20:24,932 --> 00:20:26,600
I was just asking where Lily went.

273
00:20:26,683 --> 00:20:28,143
We should call her so we can start eating.

274
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:29,978
That's right. Where is my daughter?

275
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:31,063
I'm hungry.

276
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,025
Auntie, I think this is done.

277
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:36,526
This is ready.

278
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:37,778
Where did Lily go?

279
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:46,703
[soft music playing]

280
00:21:00,092 --> 00:21:04,137
[soft music playing]

281
00:21:34,459 --> 00:21:35,627
Ivy.

282
00:21:36,795 --> 00:21:39,006
I'm sorry. You got shot because of me.

283
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:43,176
I wasn't careful enough.
Arnaldo got a hold of my gun.

284
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,511
You were hit by my own bullet.

285
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:48,515
And you know what? You were right.

286
00:21:49,474 --> 00:21:51,768
I shouldn't have let my anger
get the best of me.

287
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:56,148
I almost ruined your plans.

288
00:21:57,774 --> 00:21:59,401
You were right and I was wrong.

289
00:21:59,484 --> 00:22:02,863
Jepoy, you don't have to apologize.

290
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:07,868
Truth is, I'm at fault too,

291
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:11,121
because I didn't tell you anything.

292
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:13,582
I kept my plans from you.

293
00:22:16,585 --> 00:22:18,211
But, just like what I said earlier,

294
00:22:18,295 --> 00:22:22,591
thank you for doing everything
you can to protect me.

295
00:22:22,966 --> 00:22:25,802
So please never blame yourself

296
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:29,306
because you've done so much for me, Jepoy.

297
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,767
And those scars…

298
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:34,019
They will forever be there.

299
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:36,271
I'm sorry.

300
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:39,232
This is nothing, Ivy.

301
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:44,696
I'm willing to do everything for you.

302
00:22:59,669 --> 00:23:00,670
Uh…

303
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:07,719
Ivy, Jepoy,
everyone's been looking for you.

304
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,387
The food's ready.

305
00:23:11,348 --> 00:23:12,474
Okay.

306
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:23,944
Ivy.

307
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:28,156
<i>Don't get too comfy.</i>

308
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:31,118
<i>Just because you have something</i>
<i>doesn't mean it's yours.</i>

309
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:35,288
<i>If you hurt her, not only</i>
<i>will you get it from me…</i>

310
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:37,833
<i>I'll take her from you.</i>

311
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:47,676
Ivy, we'll go ahead.

312
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:50,095
Thanks for inviting us here.

313
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:55,559
I'll let you take Anna
to the airport tomorrow, okay?

314
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:57,269
Leave it to us.

315
00:24:00,021 --> 00:24:02,440
Be careful on your way to Singapore, okay?

316
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:05,110
Thanks for everything, Lily.

317
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:07,237
[soft music playing]

318
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,822
I'm grateful to you and Diego.

319
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:14,035
You two gave justice
to Nanny Carlotta's death.

320
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,123
I'll miss you guys.

321
00:24:22,210 --> 00:24:25,338
Anna, we'll miss you more.

322
00:24:26,923 --> 00:24:28,383
It's so hard to say goodbye

323
00:24:28,466 --> 00:24:31,636
when we're already this close,
Auntie Camia.

324
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:37,809
Anna, don't be sad.

325
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:43,190
When this is all over, I promise
we'll be together again.

326
00:24:43,273 --> 00:24:45,108
That we'll all be happy again.

327
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:47,110
Just like old times.

328
00:24:54,451 --> 00:24:56,161
Take care in Singapore.

329
00:24:58,121 --> 00:24:59,706
You should go.

330
00:24:59,789 --> 00:25:02,042
It's getting late. Take care.

331
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:03,752
Thank you, Auntie.

332
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:10,425
Anna!

333
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:24,481
[sniffles]

334
00:25:30,528 --> 00:25:32,030
We'll all be together again.

335
00:25:33,573 --> 00:25:35,116
It's a promise.

336
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:38,411
Remember that.

337
00:25:41,831 --> 00:25:43,124
It's all right. Go.

338
00:25:57,264 --> 00:25:58,974
[car engine starts]

339
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,526
[exhales]

340
00:26:13,613 --> 00:26:17,284
[party music playing]

341
00:26:33,049 --> 00:26:34,050
Mrs. Emilia.

342
00:26:53,361 --> 00:26:57,407
[pensive music playing]

343
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:05,707
[sensual music playing]

344
00:27:18,011 --> 00:27:18,845
Emilia.

345
00:27:25,810 --> 00:27:27,103
What are you doing here?

346
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:45,038
My husband and I aren't together anymore.

347
00:28:13,483 --> 00:28:15,485
Do you still love your husband, Emilia?

348
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:22,700
<i>I need a man who is my equal,</i>
<i>and that obviously isn't you!</i>

349
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:24,744
<i>Well then, let's split up already!</i>

350
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:29,749
<i>Emilia, I'd love to marry you again.</i>

351
00:28:29,833 --> 00:28:33,795
<i>Yes! I'll marry you again. Over and over.</i>

352
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:39,843
Yes.

353
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:43,179
I still love him.

354
00:28:43,263 --> 00:28:47,058
[somber music playing]

355
00:29:29,642 --> 00:29:33,104
[sobbing]

356
00:29:40,236 --> 00:29:41,571
What am I doing?

357
00:29:56,836 --> 00:29:59,005
Mom, it's late. Let's head in.

358
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:03,760
Lily, I don't think
I want this night to end.

359
00:30:03,843 --> 00:30:06,095
I want us to still be together.

360
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:15,355
Mom, all things, whether good or bad,

361
00:30:16,773 --> 00:30:18,024
have to come to an end.

362
00:30:19,692 --> 00:30:22,695
And that's why I'll cherish
this night to the fullest.

363
00:30:25,907 --> 00:30:27,867
Like I told you…

364
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:31,287
The fight has just begun.

365
00:30:31,371 --> 00:30:34,207
I'm not through with the Ardientes.

366
00:30:36,292 --> 00:30:39,295
So, I don't know when I'll see you again.

367
00:30:40,129 --> 00:30:42,090
Or, when I can be with you like this.

368
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:48,221
I won't let us be separated ever again.

369
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:51,057
Never.

370
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:05,113
[instrumental music playing]

371
00:31:25,967 --> 00:31:27,010
[scoffs]

372
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:29,304
Judge Villalobos,

373
00:31:30,263 --> 00:31:33,433
you're the one handling
my grandson's case, yes?

374
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:39,898
Well then, you know what to do.

375
00:31:43,943 --> 00:31:44,861
Good.

376
00:31:49,824 --> 00:31:54,203
[foreboding music playing]

377
00:32:06,841 --> 00:32:07,926
[whimpers]

378
00:32:13,014 --> 00:32:14,140
Sign this.

379
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:15,934
Excuse me. What's this?

380
00:32:16,017 --> 00:32:18,061
-What's that, Papa?
-I don't know.

381
00:32:18,144 --> 00:32:19,312
[clears throat]

382
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:23,733
Really? Now?

383
00:32:24,692 --> 00:32:26,527
Annulment papers?

384
00:32:29,530 --> 00:32:30,657
Annulment?

385
00:32:32,283 --> 00:32:34,077
Are you sure about that, Emilia?

386
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,579
Do you think you can just leave me?

387
00:32:36,871 --> 00:32:38,581
Can you even live without me?

388
00:32:38,665 --> 00:32:39,916
What do you think, Raul?

389
00:32:39,999 --> 00:32:41,626
I think you should reconsider this.

390
00:32:41,709 --> 00:32:43,044
You're just angry.

391
00:32:43,127 --> 00:32:44,545
I have thought it over, Raul.

392
00:32:45,129 --> 00:32:46,756
And my decision is final.

393
00:32:47,298 --> 00:32:48,424
So, sign it.

394
00:32:54,263 --> 00:32:55,390
Papa!

395
00:32:56,099 --> 00:32:57,141
What are you doing?!

396
00:32:57,225 --> 00:32:59,060
What am I doing? I'm tearing this!

397
00:33:00,103 --> 00:33:00,937
Listen!

398
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:05,942
Save your domestic drama
for some other time.

399
00:33:06,901 --> 00:33:07,986
Think of your son!

400
00:33:09,112 --> 00:33:11,656
Your son needs you all the more right now!

401
00:33:12,740 --> 00:33:15,284
And I don't want the public to know

402
00:33:15,368 --> 00:33:17,704
that this family is falling apart!

403
00:33:21,499 --> 00:33:23,668
Let's behave like a normal family.

404
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,420
Go ahead. Eat!

405
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:34,804
Thank you so much for everything.

406
00:33:35,555 --> 00:33:39,475
Miss Loring, Mr. Pandoy,
Marlon, Mr. Fernan…

407
00:33:40,601 --> 00:33:41,644
Diego.

408
00:33:42,812 --> 00:33:44,105
I'll miss you all.

409
00:33:44,188 --> 00:33:47,608
I just hope everything here
will turn out well.

410
00:33:48,401 --> 00:33:49,652
We hope so too.

411
00:33:59,662 --> 00:34:01,456
[reporter] <i>In a stunning turn of events,</i>

412
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:03,541
<i>charges against Mayor Arnaldo Torillo</i>

413
00:34:03,624 --> 00:34:05,668
<i>were dismissed as the court</i>
<i>granted his petition of…</i>

414
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:08,755
Mr. Marlon, Mr. Diego,
you should see this!

415
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:11,591
<i>…despite his confession</i>
<i>being shown to the public.</i>

416
00:34:11,674 --> 00:34:14,052
<i>He was not caught in the act</i>
<i>committing the crime.</i>

417
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:17,221
<i>Therefore, it is illegal to detain</i>
<i>the Mayor of Poblacion Ardiente</i>

418
00:34:17,305 --> 00:34:18,431
<i>by his people.</i>

419
00:34:22,143 --> 00:34:24,020
How could they get away with this?!

420
00:34:24,103 --> 00:34:27,607
[reporter] <i>Congressman, any statement</i>
<i>regarding your grandson's dismissal?</i>

421
00:34:28,775 --> 00:34:32,862
<i>Well, this isn't just a victory</i>
<i>for our family.</i>

422
00:34:33,654 --> 00:34:37,116
<i>This is a victory for</i>
<i>our country's justice system.</i>

423
00:34:38,117 --> 00:34:42,580
<i>This proves that justice is equal for all</i>

424
00:34:42,663 --> 00:34:45,124
<i>and that they continue to protect…</i>

425
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:49,253
the rights of innocent people
like my grandson.

426
00:34:50,046 --> 00:34:51,089
For the record…

427
00:34:52,298 --> 00:34:53,508
<i>We aren't bad people.</i>

428
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:56,177
<i>We aren't the enemy.</i>

429
00:34:56,886 --> 00:34:59,514
<i>We are victims</i>
<i>of unfortunate circumstances.</i>

430
00:34:59,972 --> 00:35:03,684
Geez! They freed that bastard of a mayor!

431
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:06,104
<i>Mr. Mayor, can I have a word with you?</i>

432
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:09,982
Any messages for Ms. Ivy Aguas?

433
00:35:10,066 --> 00:35:13,319
[people chanting in background]
<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

434
00:35:23,454 --> 00:35:28,251
[people chanting in background]
<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

435
00:35:28,334 --> 00:35:29,460
He's crazy…

436
00:35:29,961 --> 00:35:33,047
[people chanting in background]
<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

437
00:35:35,883 --> 00:35:39,637
[tense music playing]

438
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:44,976
[pensive music playing]

439
00:35:45,059 --> 00:35:46,269
Anna.

440
00:35:46,853 --> 00:35:48,229
Come on. I'll drive you to the airport.

441
00:35:50,690 --> 00:35:51,607
Anna?

442
00:35:51,691 --> 00:35:53,317
Jepoy, are you content?

443
00:35:53,693 --> 00:35:55,820
Are you content with the fact
that Nanny Carlota's murderer

444
00:35:55,903 --> 00:35:57,738
served only a few weeks in jail?

445
00:35:58,322 --> 00:36:01,534
Was that enough punishment for his crime?

446
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:03,703
Jepoy, is that what you call justice?!

447
00:36:03,786 --> 00:36:06,247
Anna, we won't stop
until all the Ardientes

448
00:36:06,330 --> 00:36:07,999
get the punishment they deserve!

449
00:36:08,082 --> 00:36:10,084
No. I will no longer count on anyone else

450
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:11,961
to help me find justice for Nanny Carlota!

451
00:36:12,044 --> 00:36:13,629
Anna, listen to me…

452
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:15,923
You aren't safe here.

453
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,383
I have to take you to the airport now.

454
00:36:17,466 --> 00:36:18,843
You had a deal with Ivy, remember?

455
00:36:18,926 --> 00:36:19,886
Listen to me.

456
00:36:19,969 --> 00:36:21,220
-No.
-Let's go--

457
00:36:22,889 --> 00:36:24,223
I don't care if you drag me out.

458
00:36:24,307 --> 00:36:27,768
I won't leave until Arnaldo pays!

459
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:30,646
And here I thought I was the stubborn one.

460
00:36:36,027 --> 00:36:38,988
Looks like I have to go back
to the Ardientes.

461
00:36:39,822 --> 00:36:40,865
No.

462
00:36:42,408 --> 00:36:44,076
You've already done
what you were supposed to.

463
00:36:44,619 --> 00:36:47,622
You've already exposed Arnaldo
for his crimes.

464
00:36:48,164 --> 00:36:51,209
For now, let the law take care of this.

465
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:52,501
Mom…

466
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:57,548
We both know we'd never win
against the Ardientes in court.

467
00:36:58,132 --> 00:37:01,219
And that's why
I'm working outside the law.

468
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:04,305
I'm following my own law,
what my heart says.

469
00:37:04,388 --> 00:37:06,599
Because that's the only kind
that can't be bought

470
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:08,643
or intimidated.

471
00:37:08,726 --> 00:37:10,102
And what are you going to do?

472
00:37:11,270 --> 00:37:15,191
Help Arnaldo recover right after
having him jailed?

473
00:37:16,108 --> 00:37:17,693
Mom, Arnaldo is…

474
00:37:18,194 --> 00:37:20,988
He's the Ardientes' weakness.

475
00:37:21,072 --> 00:37:25,159
Emilia's, Raul's,
and most especially Julio's.

476
00:37:25,868 --> 00:37:31,666
I'll use Arnaldo so I can bring
all those criminals down.

477
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:33,542
Lily…

478
00:37:34,043 --> 00:37:36,963
Isn't it enough
that you almost got killed?

479
00:37:41,592 --> 00:37:46,597
Mom, it's not enough
that only Arnaldo took the fall.

480
00:37:48,224 --> 00:37:50,142
Emilia has to go next.

481
00:37:51,143 --> 00:37:52,144
And Raul.

482
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:54,230
Then, finally, Julio.

483
00:37:57,942 --> 00:37:58,734
Mom…

484
00:37:59,986 --> 00:38:02,363
Do we always have to fight about this?

485
00:38:03,322 --> 00:38:07,368
Well, I won't stop if this is
what it takes to keep you safe.

486
00:38:11,664 --> 00:38:13,416
Are you really going to stop me?

487
00:38:14,750 --> 00:38:17,044
Are you really going to stop me
from taking vengeance

488
00:38:17,128 --> 00:38:21,632
on the one who killed my father
and had you raped?

489
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:23,050
Yes!

490
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:26,721
It was me who got hurt,

491
00:38:26,804 --> 00:38:29,307
so it should be my vengeance, not yours.

492
00:38:29,390 --> 00:38:31,267
But she killed my father!

493
00:38:32,601 --> 00:38:35,563
Emilia ruined my family!

494
00:38:36,689 --> 00:38:38,733
And that's why she has to go next.

495
00:38:39,734 --> 00:38:42,945
I'm not just doing this for us, Mom,

496
00:38:43,029 --> 00:38:46,032
but for all the people who were
abused by the Ardientes!

497
00:38:48,492 --> 00:38:52,455
I'll make sure whatever
suffering Emilia experiences

498
00:38:52,538 --> 00:38:55,124
will surpass Arnaldo's.

499
00:38:57,376 --> 00:38:59,128
She'll be abandoned by her husband,

500
00:38:59,545 --> 00:39:01,547
forgotten by her son,

501
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:04,550
and disowned by her father.

502
00:39:04,633 --> 00:39:06,302
She'll lose all her wealth

503
00:39:06,385 --> 00:39:08,387
and even her name as an Ardiente.

504
00:39:10,848 --> 00:39:12,266
She better prepare herself

505
00:39:13,851 --> 00:39:15,353
because I'm not afraid of her.

506
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:21,233
Only death can get in the way
of my vengeance

507
00:39:21,317 --> 00:39:23,527
against the Ardientes.

508
00:39:24,362 --> 00:39:25,613
Only death.

509
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:30,451
[tense music playing]

510
00:39:33,788 --> 00:39:34,830
Fine, then.

511
00:39:36,457 --> 00:39:38,167
I won't stop you.

512
00:39:40,669 --> 00:39:43,130
But, don't stop me with
what I'm about to do either.

513
00:39:45,424 --> 00:39:46,425
Mom.

514
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:51,472
Please don't get yourself into danger.

515
00:39:51,555 --> 00:39:55,851
I'll take the Ardientes down
the way I know how.

516
00:39:57,686 --> 00:39:58,646
Mom.

517
00:40:00,564 --> 00:40:01,690
Mom.

518
00:40:13,536 --> 00:40:15,121
[thudding]

519
00:40:18,958 --> 00:40:22,211
<i>What else do I have to do</i>
<i>to change this city?</i>

520
00:40:23,504 --> 00:40:24,505
<i>What else?</i>

521
00:40:25,881 --> 00:40:26,757
<i>What else?!</i>

522
00:40:37,768 --> 00:40:38,811
Anna?

523
00:40:39,270 --> 00:40:40,312
Auntie.

524
00:40:40,396 --> 00:40:41,355
You didn't leave?

525
00:40:45,818 --> 00:40:48,446
I haven't finished what
I came here to do, Ms. Camia.

526
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:52,324
I can't rely on the law anymore.

527
00:40:53,367 --> 00:40:56,662
I'm here now to help Ivy…

528
00:40:58,330 --> 00:41:00,082
in any way I can.

529
00:41:01,041 --> 00:41:02,126
Anna…

530
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:05,212
Every day,

531
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:12,094
my daughter risks
her life because of revenge.

532
00:41:14,221 --> 00:41:16,015
I don't want you to do the same.

533
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:21,937
We'll fight the Ardientes
in a different way.

534
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:28,611
[pensive music playing]

535
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:38,579
[cell phone ringing]

536
00:41:48,589 --> 00:41:50,674
<i>-Ivy.</i>
-Diego.

537
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:53,052
Ivy, we did everything right.

538
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:56,722
What else do we need to do
for things to change?

539
00:41:57,264 --> 00:41:58,891
For there to be justice?

540
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:01,018
This is just the beginning, Diego.

541
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:05,564
I know prison isn't the
punishment waiting for Arnaldo.

542
00:42:06,148 --> 00:42:08,192
<i>Because I know he can escape that.</i>

543
00:42:09,151 --> 00:42:11,654
That's why I only crippled Arnaldo

544
00:42:12,696 --> 00:42:15,741
to trigger the downfall of the Ardientes.

545
00:42:17,284 --> 00:42:20,454
Can you blame me
for putting my trust in the law?

546
00:42:20,996 --> 00:42:27,419
Diego, remember, the law here isn't fair.

547
00:42:28,128 --> 00:42:32,424
<i>It won't be that easy to get justice.</i>

548
00:42:32,925 --> 00:42:34,009
<i>I won't give up.</i>

549
00:42:34,093 --> 00:42:36,011
I'm with you until the end.

550
00:42:37,012 --> 00:42:41,267
Diego, it's not just me
who has faith in you…

551
00:42:42,643 --> 00:42:45,854
the people of Ardiente
place their hopes on you.

552
00:42:49,483 --> 00:42:52,111
My mother said she'll fight the Ardientes…

553
00:42:52,736 --> 00:42:54,029
<i>in the way she knows how.</i>

554
00:42:55,114 --> 00:42:58,117
If you can, protect my mother, Diego.

555
00:42:58,951 --> 00:43:00,244
Don't worry, Ivy.

556
00:43:01,120 --> 00:43:02,371
I'll keep her safe.

557
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:04,832
Thank you.

558
00:43:10,462 --> 00:43:13,007
Guys, they're here. Gather around.

559
00:43:13,591 --> 00:43:14,633
Over here.

560
00:43:15,467 --> 00:43:19,054
Ms. Camia, we're here to ask for
a statement from your party

561
00:43:19,138 --> 00:43:21,599
<i>concerning the release of Mayor Arnaldo.</i>

562
00:43:22,308 --> 00:43:24,727
<i>Thank you for accommodating us.</i>

563
00:43:25,102 --> 00:43:26,854
<i>The message we want to send</i>

564
00:43:26,937 --> 00:43:30,941
<i>is very important</i>
<i>for the people of Ardiente</i>

565
00:43:31,025 --> 00:43:33,360
<i>and to the Ardiente family.</i>

566
00:43:34,111 --> 00:43:37,698
Mayor Arnaldo's release
is a slap in the face

567
00:43:37,781 --> 00:43:40,159
to the people of Ardiente.

568
00:43:40,242 --> 00:43:42,995
<i>Like what they did with my husband's case,</i>

569
00:43:43,078 --> 00:43:47,791
<i>they've proven once more that</i>
<i>they hold the law by the neck,</i>

570
00:43:47,875 --> 00:43:50,336
<i>and that they can circumvent it.</i>

571
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:53,964
<i>This is unacceptable.</i>

572
00:43:54,048 --> 00:43:58,469
We must not let criminals
get swept into power.

573
00:43:58,886 --> 00:44:02,723
<i>Only one man has the right</i>
<i>to lead Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

574
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:07,978
<i>Only one man is ready to make</i>
<i>sacrifices for real change.</i>

575
00:44:08,646 --> 00:44:10,356
<i>That's Diego Torillo.</i>

576
00:44:11,065 --> 00:44:14,026
Let's return the power to the people.

577
00:44:14,526 --> 00:44:16,695
Long live the new Ardiente!

578
00:44:16,779 --> 00:44:19,073
[all] To the new Ardiente!

579
00:44:20,824 --> 00:44:22,951
Diego Torillo for change!

580
00:44:23,035 --> 00:44:26,038
[all] Diego Torillo for change!

581
00:44:26,121 --> 00:44:27,122
[applause]

582
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:28,749
As they say in the Olympics…

583
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:32,961
Let the games begin.

584
00:44:33,045 --> 00:44:34,129
[chuckles]

585
00:44:34,213 --> 00:44:38,300
For as long as we are
in the position of power,

586
00:44:39,134 --> 00:44:40,928
no one can touch us.

587
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:46,058
So we have to strengthen our campaign.

588
00:44:46,725 --> 00:44:50,062
We must win in this coming election.

589
00:44:50,145 --> 00:44:51,772
It's as simple as that.

590
00:44:52,106 --> 00:44:55,109
But, Papa, Arnaldo is a shell of himself.

591
00:44:55,567 --> 00:44:57,694
His reputation is already ruined.

592
00:44:58,362 --> 00:45:01,448
You know, Papa, why don't you
just make me run for governor?

593
00:45:01,532 --> 00:45:03,784
I will take the position back.
I promise you.

594
00:45:05,369 --> 00:45:06,912
[Julio laughing]

595
00:45:06,995 --> 00:45:08,330
Have you forgotten?

596
00:45:09,456 --> 00:45:12,709
People think you're dying of cancer.

597
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:16,296
Then, why don't we tell them
I was miraculously healed?

598
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:18,340
The people will even sympathize with me.

599
00:45:18,424 --> 00:45:21,009
That way, they'll vote for
me. You can buy into anything.

600
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:24,430
Quit trying to play a part in this.

601
00:45:25,264 --> 00:45:27,307
You already failed me once, Emilia.

602
00:45:27,391 --> 00:45:28,976
And that will never happen again.

603
00:45:29,059 --> 00:45:30,978
So, you're still willing
to take a risk on Arnaldo

604
00:45:31,061 --> 00:45:32,521
even if he's going crazy?!

605
00:45:32,604 --> 00:45:34,690
Arnaldo will be well again.

606
00:45:36,733 --> 00:45:40,028
And the next time you say
that your son is going crazy,

607
00:45:40,529 --> 00:45:43,198
I will send you to an asylum!

608
00:45:44,867 --> 00:45:47,077
I will make Arnaldo well again.

609
00:45:48,036 --> 00:45:50,747
And he will be the one to lead this town.

610
00:45:51,206 --> 00:45:54,543
He will be the heir to my throne. Not you.

611
00:45:56,003 --> 00:45:58,964
And certainly not that idiot, Diego.

612
00:46:00,132 --> 00:46:01,592
I promise you this.

613
00:46:02,176 --> 00:46:04,428
They would have to kill me first

614
00:46:04,511 --> 00:46:06,763
before they can take my grandson down.

615
00:46:17,900 --> 00:46:21,028
Friends, thank you so much
for supporting my event.

616
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:22,529
It was a huge success.

617
00:46:23,113 --> 00:46:24,364
You know us.

618
00:46:24,448 --> 00:46:26,408
Anything for the poor people of Ardiente.

619
00:46:26,492 --> 00:46:27,451
[chuckles]

620
00:46:27,534 --> 00:46:30,913
Congratulations
on the release of Mayor Arnaldo.

621
00:46:30,996 --> 00:46:33,165
Well, that's expected to happen.

622
00:46:34,082 --> 00:46:37,503
You know, whoever was behind
the plan to take Arnaldo down,

623
00:46:38,086 --> 00:46:40,797
didn't do his or her homework very well.

624
00:46:40,881 --> 00:46:43,800
My son was unlawfully arrested
and detained.

625
00:46:43,884 --> 00:46:45,469
That's wrong. We all know that.

626
00:46:45,552 --> 00:46:47,137
They didn't even think of that.

627
00:46:48,138 --> 00:46:49,139
Oh.

628
00:46:49,223 --> 00:46:51,391
So shallow of them not to think of that.

629
00:46:52,184 --> 00:46:53,352
Order what you want.

630
00:46:55,229 --> 00:46:57,356
[tense music playing]

631
00:46:57,439 --> 00:46:59,900
<i>You just think you've won, Emilia.</i>

632
00:47:00,526 --> 00:47:02,528
<i>But everything that happened…</i>

633
00:47:03,111 --> 00:47:04,947
<i>happened because of me.</i>

634
00:47:05,030 --> 00:47:08,367
<i>It was all part of my plan.</i>

635
00:47:08,450 --> 00:47:11,495
[tense music continues]

636
00:47:12,704 --> 00:47:14,122
I think we should get the fruit platter.

637
00:47:14,206 --> 00:47:15,624
Ma'am, are you ready?

638
00:47:19,044 --> 00:47:20,462
Ma'am, are you ready to order?

639
00:47:20,546 --> 00:47:23,131
Why are you rushing me?
Is there a taxi meter?

640
00:47:23,465 --> 00:47:25,592
Don't you know who I am?
I'm Emilia Ardiente.

641
00:47:25,676 --> 00:47:27,010
You're unbelievable!

642
00:47:31,598 --> 00:47:33,934
Wait. Can you just excuse me for a while?

643
00:47:34,017 --> 00:47:35,227
-All right.
-Order what you want.

644
00:47:35,310 --> 00:47:39,606
[tense music playing]

645
00:47:44,486 --> 00:47:45,487
Guards!

646
00:47:46,113 --> 00:47:47,447
-Guards!
-Ma'am.

647
00:47:49,116 --> 00:47:52,077
Ivy's here. Search the whole place.

648
00:47:52,744 --> 00:47:55,455
And when you find her, kill her.

649
00:47:55,956 --> 00:47:58,625
We'll make it look like
an accident if she fights back.

650
00:47:58,709 --> 00:47:59,668
-Yes, ma'am.
-Give me your gun.

651
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:01,253
Hurry!

652
00:48:18,145 --> 00:48:19,605
[laughing]

653
00:48:20,063 --> 00:48:23,442
Hey. Got you, Ivy.

654
00:48:23,525 --> 00:48:24,776
Hmm…

655
00:48:24,860 --> 00:48:26,403
Where are you?

656
00:48:26,486 --> 00:48:28,530
I can smell you.

657
00:48:28,614 --> 00:48:31,158
Hmm… That stinky perfume.

658
00:48:31,742 --> 00:48:37,080
Ivy. Come on. Stop playing games with me.

659
00:48:37,164 --> 00:48:38,290
Where are you?

660
00:48:38,832 --> 00:48:40,500
I have your lipstick.

661
00:48:41,835 --> 00:48:43,629
I know you're just here.

662
00:48:44,212 --> 00:48:46,173
Where are you?

663
00:48:46,256 --> 00:48:47,507
[laughing]

664
00:48:47,591 --> 00:48:50,969
I know you're here.
Don't let me catch you.

665
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:52,971
Where are you?!

666
00:48:54,556 --> 00:48:56,767
Come on. Ivy?

667
00:48:59,895 --> 00:49:00,812
Ivy!

668
00:49:00,896 --> 00:49:03,231
[tense music swelling]

669
00:49:11,990 --> 00:49:17,412
[tense music swelling]

670
00:49:22,501 --> 00:49:25,045
<i>Arnaldo. Arnaldo. Arnaldo.</i>

671
00:49:25,128 --> 00:49:27,923
<i>You have to accept the fact</i>
<i>that Arnaldo is not well!</i>

672
00:49:28,006 --> 00:49:31,134
<i>No one tells Julio Ardiente what to do!</i>

673
00:49:31,218 --> 00:49:33,303
<i>I'll be able to protect you more</i>

674
00:49:33,387 --> 00:49:35,055
<i>if I stay with the Ardientes.</i>

675
00:49:35,138 --> 00:49:39,351
<i>Don't you dare go near my son!</i>
<i>We aren't done yet.</i>

676
00:49:39,434 --> 00:49:41,895
[Ivy] <i>You don't deserve to die.</i>

677
00:49:41,978 --> 00:49:44,022
<i>You deserve a fate worse than death.</i>

678
00:49:44,106 --> 00:49:49,027
<i>An Ardiente never loses.</i>
<i>An Ardiente never dies!</i>

679
00:49:49,820 --> 00:49:51,071
[clatters]

680
00:49:51,154 --> 00:49:52,572
<i>Mrs. Emilia!</i>

681
00:49:53,407 --> 00:49:55,617
[screaming]

682
00:49:55,701 --> 00:49:57,577
[theme music playing]
